cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this book, please cite it as below."
title: "Learning to Love dplR: Or Using R for Tree-Ring Analysis"
abstract: >-
  A book about doing tree-ring analysis in R with the dplR package. It covers
  reading and checking ring-width data, detrending, chronology statistics and
  chronology building, regional curve and signal-free standardization,
  crossdating, time series methods, and tree-level and disturbance work, with
  an emphasis on what each method does and when it misleads. Two ITRDB
  collections run through the book. It grew out of dplR workshop notes.
authors:
  - family-names: Bunn
    given-names: "Andrew G."
    affiliation: "Western Washington University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9027-2162"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OpenDendro/learningToLoveDplR"
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
keywords:
  - dendrochronology
  - tree rings
  - dplR
  - crossdating
  - detrending
  - chronology
  - R
version: "0.1.0"
